        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile sample of brocaded silk taffeta, Spitalfields, London, 1750-1775"@en , "Textile sample of brocaded silk taffeta. With a design of broad vertical stripes with gold grounds edged with silver across which a spray of flowers twist. There are three similar stripes in the width of the textile. Between the broad stripes are narrower stripes alternating in gold and white with black and blue borders. The silk has a strip at the top and the lower edges. Beyond the strip of plain textile is a narrow warp fringe.\n\nThe textile is brocaded in coloured silk and silver threads. The gold ground of the broader strips equals a pattern weft of silver gilt strip on a ground of floating yellow and white silk warp threads. The narrow stripes are woven with an additional flushing warp whose threads are white, blue and black. The selvedge on each side is 0.7 cm of plain taffeta with two outer cordonnets."@en ;
